# PRETTIER READS THE ROOT `.gitignore` AND NO OTHER ONE (measured on 3.8.3:
# a malformed file under `.claude/` is skipped, the same file under
# `apps/marketing/scripts/screenshots/lighthouse/` is flagged). So every
# entry in a NESTED `.gitignore` has to be mirrored here or it makes
# `format:check` red while CI stays green — git never sees the file, and
# prettier always does. Both entries below exist for that reason.
apps/marketing/scripts/screenshots/lighthouse/

# Lighthouse artefacts. The CLI writes its temp output to the Windows path it
# was handed, which arrives here as a single directory whose NAME contains
# backslashes ("C:\Users\...\lighthouse.<pid>"). `.gitignore` already has
# `C:*`, so git never sees them — but prettier reads THIS file and not that
# one, so without the pattern here `format:check` is red before anybody has
# touched the repo, and a gate that starts red is a gate people learn to skip.
C:*
